{
  "kanda": "aranya",
  "sarga": 70,
  "title": "Kabandha's overlong arms are cut off",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/aranya/sarga70/aranyasans70.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/aranya/sarga70/aranyaitrans70.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "Kabandha's overlong arms are cut off when he wanted to devour Rama and Lakshmana as godsend dainty morsels. Then Kabandha wishes to know who these two are and when Lakshmana informs him of Rama, that demon feels elated for his accursed state is over at the hands of Rama."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकि रामायणे आदि काव्ये अरण्य काण्डे सप्ततितमः सर्गः",
    "Thus, this is the 70th chapter in Aranya Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the first Epic poem of India"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "3.70.1",
      "label": "3.70.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "तौ तु तत्र स्थितौ दृष्ट्वा भ्रातरौ राम लक्ष्मणौ |\nबाहु पाश परिक्षिप्तौ कबन्धो वाक्यम् अब्रवीत्",
      "iast": "tau tu tatra sthitau dṛṣṭvā bhrātarau rāma lakṣmaṇau |\nbāhu pāśa parikṣiptau kabandho vākyam abravīt",
