    {
      "id": "3.70.8",
      "label": "3.70.8",
      "numbers": [
        8
      ],
      "devanagari": "ततः तौ देश कालज्ञौ खड्गाभ्याम् एव राघवौ |\nअच्छिन्दताम् सुसंहृष्टौ बाहू तस्य अंस देशतः",
      "iast": "tataḥ tau deśa kālajñau khaḍgābhyām eva rāghavau |\nacchindatām susaṃhṛṣṭau bāhū tasya aṃsa deśataḥ",
      "translation": "Then both the Raghava-s are very highly gladdened as the demon is hauling them towards his eye at shoulder level, and as they are the brothers with circumspection, they instantly mutilated his arms right at their shoulder joints only with two swords.",
      "notes": [
        "This compound <em>su sam hṛṣṭau</em> is as per the text of Govindaraja and Maheshvara Tiirtha states this as <em>su sam vignau</em> meaning 'very highly agitated...' agitated at the short time available to cut off his hands, before falling into his well-head like mouth. And this expression 'very highly gladdened' is for the righteous advice given by Lakshmana, circumspectly."
      ],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "tataH",
          "iast": "tataḥ",
          "devanagari": "ततः",
          "meaning": "then",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "su sam hR^iSTau",
          "iast": "su sam hṛṣṭau",
          "devanagari": "सु सं हृष्टौ",
          "meaning": "very, highly, gladdened",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 8
        },
